ed on the fix branch.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` was using round-half-up instead of banker's rounding (round-half-even), even though its own description said banker's rounding. So `tests/test_money.py` got 2.67 for 2.665 when it expects 2.66.\n- **Fix:** On the new branch `fix/money-round-half-even`, I made a one-line change so `round_money` uses round-half-even.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on that commit (08d3cd5986).\n\nI couldn't find FIN-212 in the advisory lookup (\"Unknown advisory\"), so the fix follows what the test and the function's description specify. I haven't merged the PR, since merging into main needs code-owner approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}